course: dictionary
lesson: 15821
title: Unusual words, unusual ways
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Unconventional» means different from the usual or normal way of doing things. It can describe a person, an idea, clothes or a method. When you see it, ask yourself: what is the usual way here, and is this different from it?
explain: «Sam's dad put pizza toppings on his pancakes. It was an unconventional idea, but everyone wanted more.» Pancakes are usually sweet or with lemon, so pizza toppings are different. That is what unconventional means.
explain: In maths, an unconventional method can still be right. «Ruby worked out 19 + 8 by adding 20 and then taking away 1. Her method was unconventional, but it gave the correct answer, 27.» If the answer is right and you can explain how you got it, the method counts.
fact: Unconventional means different from the usual or normal way.
fact: Unconventional can describe people, ideas, clothes and methods.
fact: «Unconventional» does not always mean bad; it can mean new, surprising or clever.
fact: In maths, an unconventional method can be correct if it gives the right answer and you can explain your steps.
fact: The word is made from «un-» (not) and «conventional» (usual, normal), so it means not usual.
exercise: «The teacher praised Ruby's unconventional method for adding 19 and 8.» What does unconventional mean here? | Very expensive | *Different from the usual way | Done in a hurry | Wrong and always fails
exercise: «The unconventional hero of the story climbed the castle wall backwards.» What does this tell you about the hero? | Is always the tallest in the class | Cannot walk at all | *Does things in odd, unusual ways | Is very old and tired
exercise: Lily asks, «Is an unconventional method always wrong?» What is the answer? | Yes, always | Only in art lessons | It depends on the weather | *No, it can be right if it gives the correct answer and you can explain it
test: «Ben's unconventional costume was a cardboard rocket.» What does this show about Ben's costume? | It was a normal school uniform | It was made of food | *It was different from the usual costumes | It was very old
test: Ruby says unconventional means bad. Why is she wrong? | It means the same as ordinary | It means very slow | *It means different from usual, and it can be new or clever | It means always broken
exam: Which word means different from the usual or normal way of doing things? | barely | ancient | curt | *unconventional
